From: Thingino <dev@thingino.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: mtdblock: do not auto-attach an I/O scheduler

On the T31 (X1000-class) mainline-7.1 port, registering the first
mtdblock device wedges the boot inside blk_register_queue():

  ingenic_sfc_driver_init -> spi_nor probe -> mtd_device_parse_register
    -> add_mtd_partitions -> add_mtd_device("boot")
    -> blktrans_notify_add -> add_mtd_blktrans_dev
    -> device_add_disk -> add_disk_fwnode -> __add_disk
    -> blk_register_queue -> elevator_set_default -> elevator_change
    -> elevator_switch   [hangs]

The hang is a preempt-disabled spin in elevator_switch() (no soft-lockup
or hung-task backtrace is produced). It happens before any flash access,
so it is not the SFC/PIO path. Skipping the default I/O scheduler setup
for the mtdblock queue avoids it; mtdblock works fine with "none" and the
mtdblock4 squashfs rootfs mounts normally.

Mark the mtdblock tag set with BLK_MQ_F_NO_SCHED_BY_DEFAULT so
elevator_set_default() returns early.

This is a workaround: the real fix is to understand why
elevator_switch()/blk_mq_init_sched() spins for this queue.

--- a/drivers/mtd/mtd_blkdevs.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/mtd_blkdevs.c
@@ -329,7 +329,7 @@ int add_mtd_blktrans_dev(struct mtd_blktrans_dev *new)
 		goto out_list_del;
 
 	ret = blk_mq_alloc_sq_tag_set(new->tag_set, &mtd_mq_ops, 2,
-			BLK_MQ_F_BLOCKING);
+			BLK_MQ_F_BLOCKING | BLK_MQ_F_NO_SCHED_BY_DEFAULT);
 	if (ret)
 		goto out_kfree_tag_set;
 	
